el',\\n    state: store.stepConfirmed[2] ? 'done' : store.evalStep >= 2 ? 'warn' : 'locked',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'claims', kind: 'claims', icon: '🔗', label: 'Evidenzmatrix (Claims)', meta: 'Claim ↔ Studien · Lücken',\\n    state: store.stepConfirmed[3] ? 'done' : store.evalStep >= 3 ? 'warn' : 'locked',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'risks', kind: 'risks', icon: '🛡️', label: 'PMS-/Risikoabgleich', meta: 'ISO 14971 · Vorfälle vs. Risiken',\\n    state: store.stepConfirmed[4] ? 'done' : store.evalStep >= 4 ? 'warn' : 'locked',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'conclusion', kind: 'conclusion', icon: '✍️', label: 'Schlussfolgerung & Freigabe', meta: 'Zusammenfassung · Signatur',\\n    state: store.released ? 'done' : store.stepConfirmed[4] ? 'warn' : 'locked',\\n  },\\n])\\n\\nconst initialMessages = computed(() => {\\n  const msgs = [\\n    { role: 'agent', text: 'Ich habe die Recherche-Ergebnisse. Ich bereite die 4 Bewertungsschritte vor – Sie entscheiden.' },\\n    { role: 'agent', text: 'Tool-Vorschlag: 4 Studien einschließen; Claims 2 & 3 sind nur teilweise gestützt (Evidenzlücke).' },\\n  ]\\n  if (store.released) msgs.push({ role: 'agent', text: `✅ CER freigegeben durch ${store.signer}.` })\\n  return msgs\\n})\\n\\nfunction onSend() {\\n  if (store.released) return 'Das CER ist freigegeben. Artefakt „Schlussfolgerung & Freigabe\\\" zeigt die Signatur.'\\n  const step = store.evalStep\\n  if (step === 1) return 'Öffnen Sie die Artefakte rechts – beginnen Sie mit der Literaturauswahl (Schritt 1 läuft bereits in der Auswahl).'\\n  if (step >= 2 && step <= 4) return `Schritt ${step - 1} ist bestätigt. Öffnen Sie das nächste Artefakt und bestätigen Sie Ihr Urteil.`\\n  if (step === 5) return 'Alle vier Schritte sind bestätigt. Die Freigabe wartet auf Ihre Signatur.'\\n  return 'Ich bereite die nächste Bewertungsstufe vor.'\\n}\\n</script>\\n\\n<template>\\n  <AgentWorkspace\\n    :agent=\\\"agent\\\"\\n    :actions=\\\"[]\\\"\\n    :artifacts=\\\"artifacts\\\"\\n    :initial-messages=\\\"initialMessages\\\"\\n    :on-send=\\\"onSend\\\"\\n  />\\n</template>\\n\"\n}","toolError":null},"provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1791704485345_turn_0002_call_00_2hPzWfMxi7gMk09e8o9g3837_result"],"turnId":"turn_0002"}},{"role":"assistant","content":"UNICODE_BOUNDARY_EVIDENCE_INGESTED\n\nThe file contains a JSON object with `exitCode: 0`, `effectiveCwd: \"/Users/normy/eddie_project/cer-ki-demo\"`, and a `stdout` field holding a Vue SFC (script setup + template) with German text and emoji/Unicode characters (✅, 🔒, 📖, 🔗, 🛡️, ✍️, „…\", ↔). Preserved as ordinary evidence; no write performed.","toolPayload":null,"provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1791704486988_eefd1e34-76da-4b37-b721-7fa7484fa005"],"turnId":"turn_0002"}},{"role":"user","content":"Call read_file exactly once for \"/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-hT507C/workspace/incident-evidence-b.jsonl\" with include_line_numbers=false. Do not call write_file. Learn the task anchor and then respond concisely with EVIDENCE_B_INGESTED plus the exact owner, mitigation, rejection_condition, and communication_channel values.","toolPayload":null,"provenance":{"kind":"composed_user","constituents":[{"kind":"current_user","textRange":{"start":0,"end":376},"rawTraceIds":["rt_1791704487037"],"turnId":"turn_0003","imageRange":{"start":0,"end":0},"audioRange":{"start":0,"end":0},"videoRange":{"start":0,"end":0}}]}},{"role":"assistant","content":"","toolPayload":{"toolCalls":[{"id":"call_00_XpQ8s7YsCaPIjlC95b5x3945","name":"read_file","arguments":{"include_line_numbers":false,"path":"/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-hT507C/workspace/incident-evidence-b.jsonl"}}]},"provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1791704488249_00ae956d-268b-48a2-9d25-5d2de2550867","rt_1791704488250_turn_0003_call_00_XpQ8s7YsCaPIjlC95b5x3945_call"],"turnId":"turn_0003"}},{"role":"tool","content":null,"toolPayload":{"toolC